  },
  "script": "Sailors love a ghost story, and this is the biggest one. The Philadelphia Experiment. The legend says that in 1943 the Navy made a warship, the USS Eldridge, turn invisible, and even teleport. The whole story traces back to letters a man sent a UFO writer in the 1950s. The Navy says no such experiment ever happened, and her records put her somewhere else. The Eldridge was later sold to Greece and sailed for decades. Still a great story on night watch."
 },
